#: src/activating-environments.md:1
msgid "Activating Environments"
msgstr ""

#: src/activating-environments.md:3
msgid ""
"Some tools require an activation step, such as Python virtual environments:"
msgstr ""

#: src/activating-environments.md:9
msgid ""
"Because these tools modify the environment of a running shell, it is not "
"possible for `just` to perform this activation step for you. However, there "
"are some workarounds."
msgstr ""

#: src/activating-environments.md:13
msgid ""
"The best workaround for Python environment management is to switch to [`uv`]"
"(https://docs.astral.sh/uv/). `uv` sets up the correct environment for each "
"command, so no activation step is needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/activating-environments.md:17
msgid ""
"If that isn’t possible, and for other tools, you can create a shared prelude "
"and include it in script recipes that need it. It can span multiple lines "
"and include any number of steps:"
msgstr ""

#: src/activating-environments.md:33
msgid ""
"This workaround doesn’t work with shell recipes, which spawn a new shell for "
"each command."
msgstr ""
